/*!
@defgroup etmr_qd_driver eTMR Quadrature Decoder Driver (eTMR_QD)
@ingroup etmr
@details
@brief Quadrature decoder mode driver for the eTMR peripheral.

## Overview

The QD (Quadrature Decoder) sub-module decodes quadrature encoder
signals (Phase A and Phase B) to determine rotation position and
direction. It supports both phase-encode and count-and-direction modes
with configurable input filtering and clock prescaling.

## Features

- Phase encode mode (A leads B or B leads A)
- Count and direction mode (one phase provides clock, other provides direction)
- Configurable clock prescaler (÷1 to ÷128)
- Input filter for noise rejection
- Position counter with overflow detection
- Direction status readback

## Usage Pattern

@code{.c}
#define ETMR_INST (0U)

etmr_state_t state;
etmr_user_config_t config;

/* Step 1: Initialize common driver */
eTMR_DRV_GetDefaultConfig(&config);
eTMR_DRV_Init(ETMR_INST, &config, &state);

/* Step 2: Configure quadrature decoder */
etmr_qd_config_t qdConfig = {
    .qdMode = eTMR_QUAD_PHASE_B_FOLLOW_A,
    .qdClockPrs = eTMR_QD_CLOCK_DIV_BY_1,
    .filterSampleCounter = 4U,
    .filterSamplePeriod = 2U,
};
eTMR_DRV_QuadDecodeStart(ETMR_INST, &qdConfig);

/* Step 3: Read position and direction */
uint32_t position = eTMR_DRV_QuadGetCounter(ETMR_INST);
bool direction = eTMR_DRV_GetQuadDecodeDir(ETMR_INST);

/* Step 4: Stop and de-initialize */
eTMR_DRV_QuadDecodeStop(ETMR_INST);
eTMR_DRV_Deinit(ETMR_INST);
@endcode

## API Quick Reference

| Function | Description |
|---|---|
| eTMR_DRV_QuadDecodeStart() | Start quadrature decoder mode. |
| eTMR_DRV_QuadDecodeStop() | Stop quadrature decoder mode. |
| eTMR_DRV_QuadGetCounter() | Read quadrature position counter. |
| eTMR_DRV_QuadGetState() | Get quadrature decoder state. |

*/
